EXP 17 (diagnostic, NOT FOR SHIP): override the cpp=1 row of the UBWC
metadata geometry table from the environment.

Why: with FD_DEV_FEATURES=has_8bpp_ubwc=1 the new Y probe (values, not the
vacuous non-zero counter) shows that for R8_UNORM+UBWC the pixels AND the
metadata really are written, yet both readers decode the clear value:

  cpu-dump:   data nonzero=252960/262144  meta nonzero=8160/8192
  i2b:        261120/262144 bytes MISMATCH  got=0x00
  texelFetch: 261120/262144 words MISMATCH  want=0xff000007 got=0xff000000

with has_8bpp_ubwc=0 the same probe is EXACT on both paths, so the probe,
the copies and the barriers are fine and the failure is specific to
UBWC-on-8bpp.  Two different readers agreeing on "clear colour" is the
signature of a metadata grid the hardware did not write.

fdl6_get_ubwc_blockwidth() gives cpp=1 the generic {16, 4}, while the only
other 8bpp UBWC users in the same function - PIPE_FORMAT_Y8_UNORM and the Y
plane of 2-plane YUV, which are NOT gated by has_8bpp_ubwc - get {32, 8},
and the UV plane/r8g8 get {16, 8}.  Same bytes per texel, three grids.

TU_8BPP_UBWC="<w>x<h>" replaces the generic cpp=1 row; unset or "keep" =
the table.  Used only to find out whether any grid makes 8bpp UBWC
round-trip on a740; if one does, the next step is a real quirk (a property
of the format, not of the environment).  The Y8/r8g8/2-plane-YUV special
cases return before this override, so only plain 8bpp colour (R8*) is
affected.

Apply in /var/home/armada/opencode/mesa27-src with patch -p1, revert with
patch -R -p1.  File: src/freedreno/fdl/fd6_layout.c
diff --git a/src/freedreno/fdl/fd6_layout.c b/src/freedreno/fdl/fd6_layout.c
index 19c38a2..9cafd04 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/fdl/fd6_layout.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/fdl/fd6_layout.c
@@ -71,6 +71,27 @@ fdl6_get_ubwc_blockwidth(const struct fdl_layout *layout,
 
    uint32_t cpp = fdl_cpp_shift(layout);
    assert(cpp < ARRAY_SIZE(blocksize));
+
+   /* EXP 17, NOT FOR SHIP: TU_8BPP_UBWC=<w>x<h> replaces the cpp=1 row. */
+   if (cpp == 0) {
+      static int bw = -1, bh = -1;
+      if (bw < 0) {
+         const char *e = getenv("TU_8BPP_UBWC");
+         int w = 16, h = 4;
+         if (e && !strchr(e, 'x')) {
+            /* "keep": the table verbatim */
+         } else if (e && sscanf(e, "%dx%d", &w, &h) != 2) {
+            w = 16;
+            h = 4;
+         }
+         bw = w;
+         bh = h;
+      }
+      *blockwidth = bw;
+      *blockheight = bh;
+      return;
+   }
+
    *blockwidth = blocksize[cpp].width;
    *blockheight = blocksize[cpp].height;
 }
